Add state management methods to MenuContentObjectFactory.

MenuContentObjectFactory (SingletonInterface) holds the TMENU type
to class-string mapping. Extensions can mutate via registerMenuType()
at runtime. Under long-running runtimes a mid-request mutation from
one request permanently overrides another request's menu rendering.

Add getMenuTypeMapping()/setMenuTypeMapping() so the mapping can be
snapshotted at boot and restored per request, following the precedent
of PageRenderer::getState()/updateState().

--- a/Classes/ContentObject/Menu/MenuContentObjectFactory.php
+++ b/Classes/ContentObject/Menu/MenuContentObjectFactory.php
@@ -65,4 +65,27 @@
     {
         $this->menuTypeToClassMapping[strtoupper($type)] = $className;
     }
+
+    /**
+     * Returns the current menu type to class mapping.
+     *
+     * Useful for snapshotting the boot-time state so it can be
+     * restored per request in long-running PHP runtimes.
+     *
+     * @return array<string, class-string>
+     */
+    public function getMenuTypeMapping(): array
+    {
+        return $this->menuTypeToClassMapping;
+    }
+
+    /**
+     * Replaces the menu type to class mapping.
+     *
+     * @param array<string, class-string> $mapping
+     */
+    public function setMenuTypeMapping(array $mapping): void
+    {
+        $this->menuTypeToClassMapping = $mapping;
+    }
 }
